title: '8.0: three key-proven oracles; Warpline is opt-in per project'
summary: 'Board 5: a contract node is certified by tests + Warpline admission + a reviewer agent whose key the kernel proves never signed a PICK for that node; disagreement becomes a KNOT. Founder note: a project must be declared a Warpline project; otherwise the harness runs on standard git, because the harness has value beyond Warpline.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
  - '#warpline'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D8
    decision: 'Contract nodes certified by three oracles: tests, Warpline admission, and a key-proven reviewer who never built the node'
    rationale: Build-proper-first puts identity/keys in the 8.0 kernel, so 'never built it' is provable in 8.0.
  - id: P8-D9
    decision: Warpline is opt-in per project; non-Warpline projects run on standard git with the rest of the harness unchanged
    rationale: 'Founder: "the user still has to state if they are going to have the project as a warpline project otherwise it just functions as standard git as there are other functions to this tool beyond the warpline aspect that make it valuable"'
learnings:
  - 'Consequence of P8-D9: in git-mode projects the Warpline admission oracle has no equivalent, so contract certification there is tests + key-proven reviewer + a git-side check (clean merge onto the base branch with CI green); Warpline-native spawn duties apply only in Warpline projects.'
